Help For CW Decoding

Comma lowers WPM by 1; period raises it, silently. Range: 5 to 60.
h Shows this help, including Review controls.
Plus / minus raise / lower the detection threshold where supported.
q Stops decoding and returns to the decoder menu; keeps received text.
r Opens Review at the latest text; capture continues quietly.
s Starts or stops decoding without leaving this view.
v Announces signal, frequency and selected WPM estimate.
z Runs Zero In: retunes and matches decoder pitch; changes are kept.

In Review:
c Clears received text; capture continues.
Comma / period move backward / forward through 60-character chunks.
h Shows this same CW help.
q Returns to CW decoding.
Pitch follows the radio's CW pitch setting automatically.
WPM: receive estimate; adapts automatically; unavailable for native decoding.
Text stays until cleared or YAC closes; the latest 10,000 characters are
kept. No text file is saved. WPM is kept for this YAC session.
